{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And she made him a ketonet passim.</b> As a sign that he would be the one in charge of the household and the field, after the manner of וְהִלְבַּשְׁתִּיו כֻּתָּנְתֶּךָ (Isaiah 22:21), and as they said, of blessed memory (Bava Kamma 11a): בִּגְדוֹל אָחִי כִּי הֵיכִי דְּלִשְׁתַּמְעָן מִילֵיהּ — 'the garment of my elder brother,' so that his authority be heard from it."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {0 "Sforno's Hebrew says וְעָשָׂה לוֹ (masculine 'and he made him'), following the consonantal text; the lemma as printed has the waw-consecutive form. The Aramaic quotation from Bava Kamma 82b (cf. 11a) is rendered literally: 'the garment of my elder brother, so that his [authority] be heard from it.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:33:34.579357489Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}